### **§ 25.24 Storage of beer.**

(a) _Use of brewery in production of beer or cereal beverage._ A brewery may be used only for the following purposes involving the production of beer or cereal beverages:

(a) _Taxpaid beer._ Beer of a brewer’s own production on which the tax has been paid or determined may not be stored in the brewery, except as provided in § 25.25 or § 25.213. Beer produced by other brewers may be stored at the brewery under the following conditions:

(1) For producing, packaging and storing beer, cereal beverages, vitamins, ice, malt, malt syrup, and other by-products of the brewing process, or soft drinks and other nonalcoholic beverages;

(1) Taxpaid beer will be segregated in such a manner as to preclude mixing with nontaxpaid beer;

